msgid_plural "crash axes"
msgstr[0] "hache de secours"
msgstr[1] "haches de secours"
msgstr[2] "haches de secours"

#. ~ Same stats as a hatchet (as a tool and weapon), except it has prying
#. instead of hammering.
#. ~ Description of "crash axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"A short lightweight emergency tool with a quarter circular blade, a short "
"pick opposite the blade, and an insulated handle.  Used on airplanes to chop"
" down or pry walls, or cabinets to gain access in case of fire."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "large fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "large fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "grand extincteur"
msgstr[1] "grands extincteurs"
msgstr[2] "grands extincteurs"

#. ~ Description of "large fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is an emergency fire extinguisher containing five gallons of fire "
"retardant foam.  It would be useful for putting out adjacent fires."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "fire axe"
msgid_plural "fire axes"
msgstr[0] "hache incendie"
msgstr[1] "haches incendie"
msgstr[2] "haches incendie"

#. ~ Description of "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a large, two-handed pickhead axe normally used by firefighters.  It "
"makes a powerful melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings."
msgstr ""
"Une grande hache à deux mains normalement utilisée par les pompiers. C'est "
"une arme de mêlée puissante, mais un peu lente."

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "Marrying strap for a Halligan bar."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "Halligan bar"
msgid_plural "Halligan bars"
msgstr[0] "barre Halligan"
msgstr[1] "barres Halligan"
msgstr[2] "barres Halligan"

#. ~ Description of "Halligan bar"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a heavy multiple-use tool commonly carried by firefighters, law "
"enforcement, and military rescue units.  Use it to open locked doors without"
" destroying them or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash"
" some heads in."
msgstr ""
"Un outil lourd multi usages utilisé par les pompiers, les forces de l'ordre "
"et les militaires. Utilisez le pour ouvrir des portes vérouillées ou "
"soulever des bouches d'égoûts. Vous pouvez aussi vous en servir comme arme."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "small fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "small fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "petit extincteur"
msgstr[1] "petits extincteurs"
msgstr[2] "petits extincteurs"

#. ~ Description of "small fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a hand held fire extinguisher containing a liter of highly "
"compressed CO2 gas.  It would be useful for putting out adjacent fires."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "throwable fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extincteur lançable"
msgstr[1] "extincteurs lançables"
msgstr[2] "extincteurs lançables"

#. ~ Description of "throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a fire extinguisher in grenade form.  While not as effective as a "
"regular fire extinguisher, you can use it from a distance.  It has a plastic"
" plug that can be pulled, but is primarily activated by heat, so just throw "
"it into the flames."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "Pull plug"
msgstr "Dégoupiller"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "You pull the plug on the extinguisher grenade."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "active throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "active throwable fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "active throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is an active extinguisher grenade, likely to burst any second now.  "
"Better throw it!"
msgstr ""

#. ~  If the pole itself has a diameter of around 3 cm which is thick, to be
#. frank, then we half it for the radius -> 1,5 cm, square it -> 2,25,
#. mulitplicate with pi -> ~7,07 cm² multiplicate with 160 cm length -> 1130
#. cm³ which is 1,13 liters. We add the hook which is around 100 ml of volume.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "pike pole"
msgid_plural "pike poles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~  If the pole itself has a diameter of around 3 cm which is thick, to be
#. frank, then we half it for the radius -> 1,5 cm, square it -> 2,25,
#. mulitplicate with pi -> ~7,07 cm² multiplicate with 160 cm length -> 1130
#. cm³ which is 1,13 liters. We add the hook which is around 100 ml of volume.
#. ~ Description of "pike pole"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"A durable tool consisting of a sturdy fiberglass shaft tipped with a small "
"steel hook."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "New York hook"
msgid_plural "New York hooks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "New York hook"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"A shaft with a pair of hooks on one end and a pry bar on the other, forged "
"from a single piece of steel."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "plastic fish trap"
msgid_plural "plastic fish traps"
msgstr[0] "piège à poissons en plastique"
msgstr[1] "pièges à poissons en plastique"
msgstr[2] "pièges à poissons en plastique"

#. ~ Description of "plastic fish trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"This is a makeshift fish trap made from plastic bottles.  It's simple, even "
"primitive, but easy to use.  The principle of action: the fish swims inside "
"for bait, but can't get out.  Not humane, prohibited by law, but there are "
"no cops left to care."
msgstr ""
"Un piège à poisson fabriqué à partir de bouteilles en plastique. Primitif "
"mais facile à utiliser. Le poisson rentre pour manger l'appât et ne peut "
"plus en ressortir. Interdit par la loi, mais il n'y a plus de loi à "
"respecter."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "basket fish trap"
msgid_plural "basket fish traps"
msgstr[0] "nasse végétale"
msgstr[1] "nasses végétales"
msgstr[2] "nasses végétales"

#. ~ Description of "basket fish trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"This is a long, wicker fish trap made from bark, reeds, cordage or other "
"natural materials.  It's a staple fishing tool in many pre-industrial "
"societies.  The principle of action: the fish swims inside for bait, but "
"can't get out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "fishing hook"
msgid_plural "fishing hooks"
msgstr[0] "hameçon"
msgstr[1] "hameçons"
msgstr[2] "hameçons"

#. ~ Description of "fishing hook"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "A simple fishing hook."
msgstr "Un simple hameçon de pêche."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "improvised fishing hook"
msgid_plural "improvised fishing hooks"
msgstr[0] "hameçon de fortune"
msgstr[1] "hameçons de fortune"
msgstr[2] "hameçons de fortune"

#. ~ Description of "improvised fishing hook"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "An improvised fishing hook carved from wood or bone."
msgstr "Un hameçon improvisé dans du bois ou des ossements."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "basic fishing rod"
msgid_plural "basic fishing rods"
msgstr[0] "canne à pêche de base"
msgstr[1] "cannes à pêche de base"
msgstr[2] "cannes à pêche de base"

#. ~ Description of "basic fishing rod"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"'Fishing rod' might be a bit too charitable of a description.  In truth, "
"this is a stick with a piece of string and a hook."
msgstr ""
"'Canne à pêche' est un bien grand terme pour le décrire. En vérité, c'est "
"juste un bâton avec une ficelle et un hameçon."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "pro fishing rod"
msgid_plural "pro fishing rods"
msgstr[0] "canne à pêche pro"
msgstr[1] "cannes à pêche pro"
msgstr[2] "cannes à pêche pro"

#. ~ Description of "pro fishing rod"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"A professional fishing rod with a matching set of weights.  With this you "
"should be able to catch 'em all."
msgstr ""
"Une canne à pêche professionnelle avec un ensemble de poids correspondant. "
"Avec cela, vous devriez pouvoir tous les attraper."

#. ~ based on the ka-bar kaster
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "plastic hand fishing reel"
msgid_plural "plastic hand fishing reels"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ based on the ka-bar kaster
#. ~ Description of "plastic hand fishing reel"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"A commercial version of what is often known as a 'hobo fishing reel'.  It is"
" a short rod with a section on one end with fishing line wrapped around it, "
"with a rotating guard around that.  It is not as effective as a normal "
"fishing pole, but is much more compact than them."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "hobo hand fishing reel"
msgid_plural "hobo hand fishing reels"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "hobo hand fishing reel"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"What is often known as a 'hobo fishing reel'.  It is a short wooden rod with"
" a section on one end with fishing line wrapped around it, with a notch to "
"put the string to help pull in fish.  It is not as effective as a normal "
"fishing pole, but is much more compact than them."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "hand press"
msgid_plural "hand presses"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "hand press"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid ""
"This is a small hand press for hand loading firearm ammunition.  It comes "
"with everything you need to start hand loading your own munitions."
msgstr ""
"Une petite presse à main pour recharger vos munitions. Elle est accompagnée "
"d'un lot de matrices pour tous les types de munitions."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "makeshift shotshell 'press'"
msgid_plural "makeshift shotshell 'presses'"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "makeshift shotshell 'press'"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid ""
"This is a collection of items improvised for field reloading of shotshells."
"  A plank with a hole cut in the center, a medium-sized nail, and a whittled"
" dowel are used to seat wads, decap primers, and reprime (carefully!) hulls."
"  Powder and shot are measured with a cut down fired shotshell.  The "
"opposite side of the plank has been shaped to allow for roll crimping of the"
" plastic hulls.  There's no provision for resizing, so reloaded hulls will "
"fire best in the firearm they were fired from."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "kinetic bullet puller"
msgid_plural "kinetic bullet pullers"
msgstr[0] "extracteur de balle cinétique"
msgstr[1] "extracteurs de balle cinétiques"
msgstr[2] "extracteurs de balle cinétiques"

#. ~ Description of "kinetic bullet puller"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "This is a tool used for properly disassembling firearm ammunition."
msgstr "Un outil pour démonter les munitions d'armes à feu."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal gasoline tank"
msgid_plural "internal gasoline tanks"
msgstr[0] "réservoir à essence interne"
msgstr[1] "réservoirs à essence internes"
msgstr[2] "réservoirs à essence internes"

#. ~ Description of "internal gasoline tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "Internal tank for gasoline fuel cell bionic."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal ethanol tank"
msgid_plural "internal ethanol tanks"
msgstr[0] "réservoir à éthanol interne"
msgstr[1] "réservoirs à éthanol internes"
msgstr[2] "réservoirs à éthanol internes"

#. ~ Description of "internal ethanol tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "Internal ethanol tank for ethanol burner bionic."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal oil tank"
msgid_plural "internal oil tanks"
msgstr[0] "réservoir à essence interne"
msgstr[1] "réservoirs à essence internes"
msgstr[2] "réservoirs à essence internes"

#. ~ Description of "internal oil tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "Internal oil tank for oil generator bionic."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal battery compartment"
msgid_plural "internal battery compartments"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "internal battery compartment"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid ""
"Internal compartment for holding medium sized batteries for battery system "
"bionic."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "copper knife"
msgid_plural "copper knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau en cuivre"
msgstr[1] "couteaux en cuivre"
msgstr[2] "couteaux en cuivre"

#. ~ Description of "copper knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"A knife consisting of crudely-worked copper, and a simple handle.  "
"Primitive, but a step above stone-age."
msgstr ""
"Un couteau en cuivre rudimentaire doté d'une garde. Un outil primitif, mais "
"meilleur qu'un outil néolithique."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "bronze knife"
msgid_plural "bronze knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau en bronze"
msgstr[1] "couteaux en bronze"
msgstr[2] "couteaux en bronze"

#. ~ Description of "bronze knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"Cast bronze knife with a full tang, with a handle wrapped in cord and "
"leather, lovingly work-hardened and sharpened to a fine edge."
msgstr ""
"Un couteau en bronze forgé, équipé d'une poignée enrobée de cuir et de corde"
" et doté d'une lame affutée laborieusement."

#. ~ Too small to be effectively used for butchering, still not bad at it due
#. to serrated edge.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "dive knife"
msgid_plural "dive knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau de plongée"
msgstr[1] "couteaux de plongée"
msgstr[2] "couteaux de plongée"

#. ~ Too small to be effectively used for butchering, still not bad at it due
#. to serrated edge.
#. ~ Description of "dive knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a short, sturdy knife with a serrated edge for cutting lines and "
"straps, and a blunt tip for prying.  Used primarily by divers, this knife "
"has been fitted with cork to slow its descent if dropped underwater, so it "
"takes up more space than usual."
msgstr ""
"Un petit couteau solide dotée d'une lame dentelée utilisée pour couper à "
"travers des cordages ou de lignes de cable, sa pointe étant arrondie et "
"renforcée pour être utilisée comme outil de forçage. Principalement utilisé "
"par les plongeurs, un flotteur est attaché pour l'empécher de couler trop "
"vite lorsqu'il est lâché, le rendant un peu plus encombrant qu'attendu."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "honey scraper"
msgid_plural "honey scrapers"
msgstr[0] "grattoir à miel"
msgstr[1] "grattoirs à miel"
msgstr[2] "grattoirs à miel"

#. ~ Description of "honey scraper"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"A sharp, knife-like tool used in harvesting honey from beehives.  Makes a "
"passable melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un outil ressemblant à un couteau utiliser pour gratter le miel de morceau "
"de ruche. Bien qu'il ne soit pas conçu pour, il peut être décemment utile "
"comme arme."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "pocket knife"
msgid_plural "pocket knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau de poche"
msgstr[1] "couteaux de poche"
msgstr[2] "couteaux de poche"

#. ~ Description of "pocket knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a small pocket knife.  It isn't great for combat, but it's better "
"than nothing.  It's sharp enough to butcher with."
msgstr ""
"Un petit couteau de poche. il n'est pas génial pour le combat, mais c'est "
"mieux que rien. Il est assez pointu pour vous aider à dépecer des corps."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "stone knife"
msgid_plural "stone knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau en pierre"
msgstr[1] "couteaux en pierre"
msgstr[2] "couteaux en pierre"

#. ~ Description of "stone knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a sharpened stone set into a hollowed handle.  Not nearly as usable "
"as a proper knife, but it's better than nothing."
msgstr ""
"Une pierre aiguisée avec un manche taillé dedans. Pas aussi pratique qu'un "
"vrai couteau, mais c'est mieu que rien."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "boxcutter knife"
msgid_plural "boxcutter knives"
msgstr[0] "cutter"
msgstr[1] "cutters"
msgstr[2] "cutters"

#. ~ Description of "boxcutter knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a small knife, designed for opening boxes.  It could cause some "
"damage, but it really should be used against inanimate objects.  It is too "
"small to butcher corpses with."
msgstr ""
"Un petit couteau repliable, communément utilisé pour ouvrir des boites en "
"cartons. Capable de blesser assez bien quelques ennemis, il serait "
"probablement une meilleure idée d'utiliser sa lame uniquement contre des "
"objets inanimés dû à sa petite taille et à sa fragilité. La lame est trop "
"courte pour être utilisée comme outil de boucherie."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "stone chopper"
msgid_plural "stone choppers"
msgstr[0] "hachoir en pierre"
msgstr[1] "hachoirs en pierre"
msgstr[2] "hachoirs en pierre"

#. ~ Description of "stone chopper"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"A rock with sharpened edges, produced by knapping.  Works as a crude cutting"
" and butchering tool, if nothing else is available."
msgstr ""
"Une pierre dotée de bords pointus produits par taillage. Peut servir comme "
"un outil rudimentaire de boucherie ou pour couper quelque chose si vous "
"n'avez rien de mieux."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "digging stick"
msgid_plural "digging sticks"
msgstr[0] "bâton-pelle"
msgstr[1] "bâton-pelles"
msgstr[2] "bâton-pelles"

#. ~ Description of "digging stick"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a large stick, with the end carved into a broad blade for digging.  "
"It could be used to dig shallow pits, but not deep ones."
msgstr ""
"C'est un gros bâton dont la pointe a été taillée en une bêche large pour "
"creuser. Il pourrait être utilisé pour creuser des fossés peu profonds mais "
"pas plus."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "trowel"
msgid_plural "trowels"
msgstr[0] "déplantoir"
msgstr[1] "déplantoirs"
msgstr[2] "déplantoirs"

#. ~ Description of "trowel"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A small, sharp gardening shovel, perfect for digging up grubs and worms."
msgstr ""
"Une petite pelle de jardinage, parfaite pour déterrer les larves et les "
"vers."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "hoe"
msgid_plural "hoes"
msgstr[0] "houe"
msgstr[1] "houes"
msgstr[2] "houes"

#. ~ Description of "hoe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a farming implement.  You can use it to turn tillable land into a "
"slow-to-cross pile of dirt, or dig a shallow pit."
msgstr ""
"Un outil de jardinage. Vous pouvez l'utiliser pour créer un monticule de "
"terre ou un fossé peu profond à partir d'un terrain labourable."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "bronze hoe"
msgid_plural "bronze hoes"
msgstr[0] "houe en bronze"
msgstr[1] "houes en bronze"
msgstr[2] "houes en bronze"

#. ~ Description of "bronze hoe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a farming implement made from bronze.  The added heft and durability"
" should let you till soil for farming more easily as well."
msgstr ""
"Un outil de jardinage en bronze. Le poids additionnel de la tête comparément"
" à l'acier devrait rendre son utilisation pour labourer plus facile."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "wooden shovel"
msgid_plural "wooden shovels"
msgstr[0] "pelle en bois"
msgstr[1] "pelles en bois"
msgstr[2] "pelles en bois"

#. ~ Description of "wooden shovel"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a crude shovel with shovelhead made from wood, historically used as "
"an alternative to metal shovels when metal was too expensive.  It works "
"passably well, but really can't compare to a metal shovel."
msgstr ""
"Une pelle rudimentaire ayant une tête en bois, historiquement utilisée comme"
" alternative au pelles en métal lors ce que celui-ci était trop cher. Bien "
"qu'elle soit décente pour creuser, une vraie pelle en métal serait "
"préférable."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "metal rake"
msgid_plural "metal rakes"
msgstr[0] "râteau en métal"
msgstr[1] "râteaux en métal"
msgstr[2] "râteaux en métal"

#. ~ Description of "metal rake"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "A sturdy metal rake, a must-have during autumn."
msgstr ""
"Un râteau à feuilles solide en métal, un outil essentiel pour l'automne."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "plastic rake"
msgid_plural "plastic rakes"
msgstr[0] "râteau en plastique"
msgstr[1] "râteaux en plastique"
msgstr[2] "râteaux en plastique"

#. ~ Description of "plastic rake"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A cheap plastic rake.  Will break quite fast if used for anything other than"
" raking leaves."
msgstr ""
"Un râteau à feuilles bon marché en plastique. Il se cassera très vite si "
"vous décidez de l'utiliser pour quoi que ce soit d'autre que ramasser des "
"feuilles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "scythe"
msgid_plural "scythes"
msgstr[0] "faux"
msgstr[1] "faux"
msgstr[2] "faux"

#. ~ Description of "scythe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is an old-fashioned farming tool used to cut tall grass.  While it may "
"be a giant blade on the end of a stick, it is incredibly awkward to use for "
"anything but its intended purpose."
msgstr ""
"Un vieil outil de moisson ou de désherbage. Bien que cet outil soit juste "
"une lame attachée à un bâton, l'utiliser comme arme est assez difficile."

#. ~ Description of "scythe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of an old-fashioned farming tool used "
"to cut tall grass."
msgstr "Une réplique bon marché et émoussée d'un vieil outil de moissonnage."

#. ~ Item name
