msgid_plural "remote vehicle controllers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "remote vehicle controller"
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"A remote controller for real cars.  Can turn onboard devices on and off.  "
"Some cars can be driven remotely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "birchbark funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a small birchbark funnel.  Place it above an outdoor container to "
"collect rainwater."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "birchbark funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the birchbark funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside and place a "
"container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr ""
"Ceci est un entonnoir utilisé pour récolter l'eau de pluie. Activez le en "
"extérieur et placez un contenant dessous pour collecter l'eau de pluie."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr ""
"Vous mettez en place l'entonnoir, il est prêt à collecter l'eau de pluie."

#. ~ Description of "leather funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a small, leather funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside "
"and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr ""
"Un petit entonnoir en cuir pour collecter l'eau de pluie. Utilisez le à "
"l'extérieur et placez un conteneur dessour pour collecter l'eau."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "leather funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the leather funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr ""
"Vous mettez en place l'entonnoir en cuir, il est prêt à collecter l'eau de "
"pluie."

#. ~ Description of "makeshift funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a small, makeshift funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside"
" and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr ""
"Ceci est un petit entonnoir de fortune, utilisé pour récolter l'eau de "
"pluie. Activez le en extérieur et placez un contenant dessous pour collecter"
" l'eau de pluie."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "makeshift funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the makeshift funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr ""
"Vous mettez en place l'entonnoir de fortune, il est prêt à collecter l'eau "
"de pluie."

#. ~ Description of "metal funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a large metal funnel used to collect rainwater.  Less portable than "
"plastic funnels, but collects more water.  Use it outside and place a "
"container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un grand entonnoir en métal utilisé pour collecter l'eau de "
"pluie. Moins portable que les entonnoirs en plastique, mais collecte plus "
"d'eau. Utilisez-le à l'extérieur et placez un récipient en dessous pour "
"recueillir l'eau lorsqu'il pleut."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "metal funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the metal funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr ""
"Vous placez l'entonnoir en métal dans l'attente de collecter la pluie."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "tarp raincatcher"
msgid_plural "tarp raincatchers"
msgstr[0] "collecteur d'eau à bâche"
msgstr[1] "collecteurs d'eau à bâche"
msgstr[2] "collecteurs d'eau à bâche"

#. ~ Description of "tarp raincatcher"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"Some sticks and string with a tarpaulin to set up an improvised raincatcher."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "tarp raincatcher"
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You set up the raincatcher, waiting to collect water."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "barometer"
msgid_plural "barometers"
msgstr[0] "baromètre"
msgstr[1] "baromètres"
msgstr[2] "baromètres"

#. ~ Description of "barometer"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "A plastic barometer that can read the atmospheric pressure."
msgstr "Un baromètre en plastique qui vous indique la pression atmosphérique."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "goo canister"
msgid_plural "goo canisters"
msgstr[0] "boîte de limon gluant"
msgstr[1] "boîtes de limon gluant"
msgstr[2] "boîtes de limon gluant"

#. ~ Description of "goo canister"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"There is a label on this canister: \"Warning: contains highly toxic and "
"corrosive materials.  Contents may be sentient.  Open at your own risk.\" "
"You think you can feel something moving inside it."
msgstr ""
"Il y a une étiquette sur cette boîte: \"Attention: contient des matériaux "
"hautement toxiques et corrosifs. Ouvrez à vos risques et périls.\" Vous avez"
" l'impression que quelque chose bouge à l'intérieur."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "chemistry set"
msgid_plural "chemistry sets"
msgstr[0] "kit de chimie"
msgstr[1] "kits de chimie"
msgstr[2] "kits de chimie"

#. ~ Description of "chemistry set"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a chemistry set stored in a box.  The contents include glass "
"containers, hoses, metal wire, a hotplate, and safety glasses.  It might be "
"used to craft some chemistry projects if you're so inclined."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un ensemble de chimie rangé dans une boîte. Il contient des "
"récipients en verre, des tuyaux, du fil métallique, une plaque chauffante et"
" des lunettes de sécurité. Vous pouvez l'utiliser pour réaliser des travaux "
"de chimie si vous en avez envie."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "basic chemistry set"
msgid_plural "basic chemistry sets"
msgstr[0] "kit de chimie basique"
msgstr[1] "kits de chimie basique"
msgstr[2] "kits de chimie basique"

#. ~ Description of "basic chemistry set"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a basic chemistry set which includes glass containers, hoses and "
"safety glasses.  It might be used to craft some chemistry projects if you're"
" so inclined, but you'll need a source of heat."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un ensemble de base pour la chimie qui comprend des récipients "
"en verre, des tuyaux et des lunettes de sécurité. Vous pouvez l'utiliser "
"pour réaliser des travaux de chimie si vous en avez envie, mais vous aurez "
"besoin d'une source de chaleur."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json data/mods/innawood/items/electronics.json
msgid "electrolysis kit"
msgid_plural "electrolysis kits"
msgstr[0] "kit d'électrolyse"
msgstr[1] "kits d'électrolyse"
msgstr[2] "kits d'électrolyse"

#. ~ Description of "electrolysis kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json data/mods/innawood/items/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A set of wiring and electrodes for applying a direct current, usually to a "
"liquid.  Useful for crafting.  Load with a storage battery or 12V vehicle "
"battery to use."
msgstr ""
"Ensemble de fils et d'électrodes permettant d'appliquer un courant continu, "
"généralement à un liquide. Utile pour l'artisanat. Chargez avec une batterie"
" d'accumulateurs ou une batterie de véhicule 12V pour l'utiliser."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "ketene lamp"
msgid_plural "ketene lamps"
msgstr[0] "lampe à cétène"
msgstr[1] "lampes à cétène"
msgstr[2] "lampes à cétène"

#. ~ Description of "ketene lamp"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a section of glass pipe with a bulb in the middle, which contains an"
" electrical heating element.  It is used for producing ketene via pyrolysis "
"of acetone or 1,3-butadiene from cyclohexane, for use in other chemical "
"reactions.  Due to the instability of ketene, it can't be stored and must be"
" used immediately."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "makerspace kit for STEM"
msgid_plural "makerspace kits for STEM"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "makerspace kit for STEM"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"With hundreds of pieces and dozens of blueprints for small engineering "
"projects designed for beginner learners.  Explore mechanics and hydraulics!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "robotics kit for young learners"
msgid_plural "robotics kits for young learners"
msgstr[0] "kit de robotique pour novices"
msgstr[1] "kits de robotique pour novices"
msgstr[2] "kits de robotique pour novices"

#. ~ Description of "robotics kit for young learners"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Build and program robots with this complete robotics engineering system.  "
"Using sensors, motors, a core controller, and hundreds of snap-together "
"building pieces, you can follow the instructions to assemble 12 different "
"robots.  The versatile parts also allow you to make robots according to your"
" own designs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "stirling engine kit"
msgid_plural "stirling engine kits"
msgstr[0] "kit d'apprentissage de moteurs sterling"
msgstr[1] "kits d'apprentissage de moteurs sterling"
msgstr[2] "kits d'apprentissage de moteurs sterling"

#. ~ Description of "stirling engine kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Stirling engine kit demonstrates principles behind the generation of "
"electricity through the use of hot air."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "small vacuum oven"
msgid_plural "small vacuum ovens"
msgstr[0] "petite étuve à vide"
msgstr[1] "petites étuve à vide"
msgstr[2] "petites étuve à vide"

#. ~ Description of "small vacuum oven"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A small 0.9 cubic foot vacuum oven used to purge residual solvents out of "
"liquids and solid.  Looks kind of like a microwave."
msgstr ""
"Un petit four à vide de 0,9 pied cube utilisé pour éliminer les solvants "
"résiduels des liquides et des solides. Il ressemble un peu à un micro-ondes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "small closed loop extractor"
msgid_plural "small closed loop extractors"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "small closed loop extractor"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A small closed loop extractor used for extracting essential oils from "
"organic material producing a high quality extract.  It consists of a long "
"metal tube clamped onto a steel \"honey pot\".  Organic material is packed "
"in the tube, flushed with solvent, and essential oils gathered from the pot."
"  Must be powered up to operate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "large closed loop extractor"
msgid_plural "large closed loop extractors"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "large closed loop extractor"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A large machine used for extracting essential oils from large batches of "
"organic material producing a low quality crude oil.  It consists of three "
"long metal tubes funneled into a large drum that's set horizontally.  A "
"series of hoses and tubes come out of the machine going to different valves."
"  It needs to be powered up to operate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "makeshift essential oil extractor"
msgid_plural "makeshift essential oil extractors"
msgstr[0] "extracteur d'huiles essentielles de fortune"
msgstr[1] "extracteurs d'huiles essentielles de fortune"
msgstr[2] "extracteurs d'huiles essentielles de fortune"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift essential oil extractor"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift extraction system.  It's pretty much just a 55gal drum, a pipe "
"to stir the solution, and a faucet at the bottom to drain the extractor.  "
"Not the most ideal piece of equipment but it will work."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "catalytic cracking reactor"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift extraction system.  As makeshift as you can consider something "
"that was purpose built in a laboratory by a group of experts.  Meticulously "
"disassembled and reassembled."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "qualitative filter paper"
msgid_plural "qualitative filter paper"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "qualitative filter paper"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Filter paper for separating solids from liquids.  This filter paper has a "
"rating of 2 microns, separating more solids out than quantitative filter "
"paper but the process takes longer.  It's intended to be disposable, but you"
" could probably use it for some time before it's unusable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "quantitative filter paper"
msgid_plural "quantitative filter paper"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "quantitative filter paper"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Filter paper for separating solids from liquids.  This filter paper has a "
"rating of 20 microns, separating less solids out than qualitative filter "
"paper but the process is much faster.  It's intended to be disposable, but "
"you could probably use it for some time before it's unusable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "plastic gasket set"
msgid_plural "plastic gasket sets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "plastic gasket set"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A set of three plastic gaskets.  They're intended to be single-use, but you "
"could probably use it for some time before they're too worn out to use."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "vacuum pump"
msgid_plural "vacuum pumps"
msgstr[0] "pompe à vide"
msgstr[1] "pompes à vide"
msgstr[2] "pompes à vide"

#. ~ Description of "vacuum pump"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A small belt driven mechanical pump capable of achieving a vacuum of -29.99 "
"hg (50 microns)."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "recovery pump"
msgid_plural "recovery pumps"
msgstr[0] "pompe de récupération"
msgstr[1] "pompes de récupération"
msgstr[2] "pompes de récupération"

#. ~ Description of "recovery pump"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A medium-sized vacuum pump designed to recover solvent (hydrocarbons) from "
"extracted essential oils."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Energy efficiency is 40%, consuming 355 MJ and 8.936 L of water for 1 kg
#. of H2 and 7.936 kg of O2.
#. ~ Description of "makeshift water electrolyzer"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift appliance which decomposes water into oxygen and hydrogen via "
"electrolysis of sodium hydroxide solution.  Much less energy-efficient than "
"actual industrial equipment."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Consumes 200 MJ for 1 kg of NH3.
#. ~ Description of "makeshift ammonia machine reactor"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A huge appliance built from salvaged industrial equipment which produces "
"ammonia via the Haber-Bosch process from hydrogen and nitrogen.  As it uses "
"primitive catalysts for the reaction, energy efficiency is very low.  This "
"one is powered by electricity."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Consumes 20 MJ for 1 kg of NH3.
#. ~ Description of "makeshift ammonia machine pipework"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A rather complicated system of thick-walled pipes, powerful compressors and "
"wiring meant to interface with a reactor producing ammonia from nitrogen and"
" hydrogen via Haber-Bosch process.  It also acts as a power source for all "
"the low-powered electrical components of the system."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Uses up 1.2 MJ for 1 m^3 of N2 (1.253 kg), assuming 99.5% purity.
#. ~ Description of "makeshift nitrogen generator"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A large makeshift appliance which captures nitrogen from the air for use in "
"chemistry projects.  It includes a standard air filter for filtering out "
"dust and other large particles, a deliquescent dryer to remove water vapor "
"from air, and a nitrogen membrane filter to separate nitrogen from dry air."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "butane tank"
msgid_plural "tanks of butane"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "butane tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a tank of compressed butane.  It can be used to extract essential "
"oils from organic material."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "hydrogen tank"
msgid_plural "hydrogen tanks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "hydrogen tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a tank of compressed hydrogen gas.  If you need to make water from "
"scratch, or lift a zeppelin, it could come in handy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/containers.json
