msgstr[1] "hygromètres"
msgstr[2] "hygromètres"

#. ~ Description of "hygrometer"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "A plastic hygrometer that can read the relative humidity in the air."
msgstr ""
"Un hygromètre en plastique, qui vous indique l'humidité relative de l'air."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "nitrogen tank"
msgid_plural "nitrogen tanks"
msgstr[0] "bouteille d'azote"
msgstr[1] "bouteilles d'azote"
msgstr[2] "bouteilles d'azote"

#. ~ Description of "nitrogen tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a tank of compressed nitrogen gas.  Nitrogen is useful for its lack "
"of reactivity.  Don't try to breathe it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "oxygen cylinder"
msgid_plural "oxygen cylinders"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "oxygen cylinder"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A large steel cylinder used for storing pressurized gas.  It is marked with "
"a faded, but legible O2 symbol."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "platinum grille"
msgid_plural "platinum grilles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "platinum grille"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a metal grille with a layer of platinum plating, suitable for use as"
" a catalyst for some chemical reactions."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "portal generator"
msgid_plural "portal generators"
msgstr[0] "générateur de portail"
msgstr[1] "générateurs de portail"
msgstr[2] "générateurs de portail"

#. ~ Description of "portal generator"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a rare, bizarre, and arcane device of an otherworldly nature.  It's "
"giving you a headache just looking at it.  It is covered in alien markings."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "teleport pad"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a kit for a teleporter trap consisting of a teleporter and a solar "
"cell that is triggered when stepped upon."
msgstr ""
"C'est un kit pour un piège de téléportation qui consiste en un téléporteur "
"et une cellule photovoltaïque qui s'active quand on marche dessus."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "teleport pad"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "You place the telepad."
msgstr "Vous placez le téléporteur."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "teleporter"
msgid_plural "teleporters"
msgstr[0] "téléporteur"
msgstr[1] "téléporteurs"
msgstr[2] "téléporteurs"

#. ~ Description of "teleporter"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is an experimental device that will teleport you a short distance when "
"activated."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil expérimental qui vous téléporte aléatoirement sur une courte "
"distance quand vous l'activez."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000"
msgid_plural "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000s"
msgstr[0] "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000"
msgstr[1] "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000s"
msgstr[2] "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000s"

#. ~ Description of "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A briefcase with built-in laptop that looks like it's from the 80s.  Its "
"vintage monochrome monitor displays a plethora of meteorological data.  No "
"sign of the FLDSMDFR, however."
msgstr ""
"Une mallette avec ordinateur portable intégré qui semble sortir des années "
"80. Son écran monochrome vintage affiche une pléthore de données "
"météorologiques. Aucun signe du FLDSMDFR, cependant."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "basic laboratory analysis kit"
msgid_plural "basic laboratory analysis kits"
msgstr[0] "kit d'analyse de laboratoire de base"
msgstr[1] "kits d'analyse de laboratoire de base"
msgstr[2] "kits d'analyse de laboratoire de base"

#. ~ Description of "basic laboratory analysis kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This hefty kit contains some basic things you should probably not try to do "
"precise chemistry without: namely, a small balance scale, a "
"spectrophotometer, a melting point apparatus, a pH meter, and a set of paper"
" for thin layer chromatography.  This makes it a lot easier to feel "
"confident that the chemical you've made is what you think you've made."
msgstr ""
"Ce kit volumineux contient des éléments de base sans lesquels vous ne "
"devriez probablement pas essayer de faire de la chimie de pointe : une "
"petite balance, un spectrophotomètre, un appareil à point de fusion, un pH-"
"mètre et un jeu de papier pour la chromatographie en couche. Il est ainsi "
"beaucoup plus facile d'être sûr que le produit chimique que vous avez "
"fabriqué est bien celui que vous pensez avoir fabriqué."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "small weight scale"
msgid_plural "small weight scales"
msgstr[0] "petite balance à poids"
msgstr[1] "petites balances à poids"
msgstr[2] "petites balances à poids"

#. ~ Description of "small weight scale"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple scale that uses a set of steel weights on sliding bars to "
"measure a sample's mass quite accurately."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une balance simple qui utilise un ensemble de poids en acier sur"
" des barres coulissantes pour mesurer la masse d'un échantillon avec une "
"grande précision."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "spectrophotometer"
msgid_plural "spectrophotometers"
msgstr[0] "spectrophotomètre"
msgstr[1] "spectrophotomètres"
msgstr[2] "spectrophotomètres"

#. ~ Description of "spectrophotometer"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This ubiquitous analytical chemistry tool measures the light absorption of a"
" liquid sample in a special tube called a cuvette."
msgstr ""
"Cet outil de chimie analytique très répandu mesure l'absorption de lumière "
"d'un échantillon liquide dans un tube spécial appelé cuvette."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "set of spectrometry cuvettes"
msgid_plural "sets of spectrometry cuvettes"
msgstr[0] "ensemble de cuvettes de spectrométrie"
msgstr[1] "ensembles de cuvettes de spectrométrie"
msgstr[2] "ensembles de cuvettes de spectrométrie"

#. ~ Description of "set of spectrometry cuvettes"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a small box filled with precisely calibrated square plastic tubes "
"for laboratory spectrometer use."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une petite boîte remplie de tubes carrés en plastique calibrés "
"avec précision, destinés à être utilisés dans les spectromètres de "
"laboratoire."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "pH meter"
msgid_plural "pH meters"
msgstr[0] "pH-mètre"
msgstr[1] "pH-mètres"
msgstr[2] "pH-mètres"

#. ~ Description of "pH meter"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is basically a pair of glass probes on a voltmeter.  By putting one "
"probe into a calibration solution (conveniently included) and the other in a"
" substance, you can calculate the acidity."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit en fait d'une paire de sondes en verre sur un voltmètre. En "
"plaçant une sonde dans une solution d'étalonnage ( comprise dans l'appareil)"
" et l'autre dans une substance, vous pouvez calculer l'acidité."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "voltmeter"
msgid_plural "voltmeters"
msgstr[0] "voltmètre"
msgstr[1] "voltmètres"
msgstr[2] "voltmètres"

#. ~ Description of "voltmeter"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This device has two probes that let you measure the electrical potential "
"between two points."
msgstr ""
"This device has two probes that let you measure the electrical potential "
"between two points."

#. ~ Dimensions from a sampling of consumer digital multimeter models online.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "multimeter"
msgid_plural "multimeters"
msgstr[0] "multimètre"
msgstr[1] "multimètres"
msgstr[2] "multimètres"

#. ~ Dimensions from a sampling of consumer digital multimeter models online.
#. ~ Description of "multimeter"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This gadget is a little bigger than a handheld calculator, with a digital "
"display and two pointed probes connected by wires.  It can measure not just "
"voltage, but current in amps, and resistance in ohms, as well as test for "
"electrical continuity."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "melting point apparatus"
msgid_plural "units of melting point apparatus"
msgstr[0] "Appareil de mesure du point de fusion"
msgstr[1] "Appareils de mesure du point de fusion"
msgstr[2] "Appareils de mesure du point de fusion"

#. ~ Description of "melting point apparatus"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is basically a hot plate, with a metal housing attached.  The metal "
"housing has a magnification viewport and a slot into which a capillary tube "
"containing a crystallized sample is inserted.  The device lets you precisely"
" measure the melting point of a crystal, a property very useful in "
"identifying what it is and how pure it is."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit en fait d'une plaque chauffante, à laquelle est fixé un boîtier "
"métallique. Le boîtier métallique comporte un hublot de grossissement et une"
" fente dans laquelle on insère un tube contenant un échantillon cristallisé."
" L'appareil vous permet de mesurer avec précision le point de fusion d'un "
"cristal, une propriété très utile pour identifier sa composition et son "
"degré de pureté."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "vortex device"
msgid_plural "vortex devices"
msgstr[0] "appareil à vibrations"
msgstr[1] "appareils à vibrations"
msgstr[2] "appareils à vibrations"

#. ~ Description of "vortex device"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a small, hefty, boring looking machine.  Its weighted trapezoidal "
"frame has a single on-off switch and a speed dial, and on top of it sits a "
"rubber receptacle.  Pressing a test tube into the receptacle would, with "
"power, rapidly shake and mix the contents of the test tube.  It's "
"surprisingly fun to use."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une petite machine, lourde et au demeurant banale. Son cadre "
"trapézoïdal lesté est doté d'un seul interrupteur marche-arrêt et d'un "
"cadran de vitesse, et sur le dessus se trouve un réceptacle en caoutchouc. "
"En appuyant sur un tube à essai dans le réceptacle, on peut secouer et "
"mélanger rapidement le contenu du tube à essai. C'est étonnamment amusant à "
"utiliser."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "light detector"
msgid_plural "light detectors"
msgstr[0] "capteur de lumière"
msgstr[1] "capteurs de lumière"
msgstr[2] "capteurs de lumière"

#. ~ Description of "light detector"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a photodiode on a chip, designed to convert incoming light to "
"electrical energy for quantification."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "glass prism"
msgid_plural "glass prisms"
msgstr[0] "prisme en verre"
msgstr[1] "prismes en verre"
msgstr[2] "prismes en verre"

#. ~ Description of "glass prism"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a high quality crystal glass prism for separating and redirecting "
"light."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Volume here is displacement volume of a corked 25mL test tube.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "small glass tube"
msgid_plural "small glass tubes"
msgstr[0] "petit tube en verre"
msgstr[1] "petits tubes en verre"
msgstr[2] "petits tubes en verre"

#. ~ Volume here is displacement volume of a corked 25mL test tube.
#. ~ Description of "small glass tube"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a small glass tube.  What more could you possibly want to know about"
" it?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "microscope"
msgid_plural "microscopes"
msgstr[0] "microscope"
msgstr[1] "microscopes"
msgstr[2] "microscopes"

#. ~ Description of "microscope"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A classic tool for the ages!  This hefty, durable piece of lab equipment "
"makes small things look bigger.  Without electricity the light doesn't work,"
" but the rest of it is surprisingly functional.  Unfortunately it's not "
"useful for very much at the moment."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "dissecting microscope"
msgid_plural "dissecting microscopes"
msgstr[0] "microscope de dissection"
msgstr[1] "microscopes de dissection"
msgstr[2] "microscopes de dissection"

#. ~ Description of "dissecting microscope"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This microscope has less magnification than a standard one.  It's also "
"stereoscopic and produces a neat 3D image of the surface.  It was typically "
"used for doing dissections and other fine detail work on small creatures.  "
"It still works pretty well with an added light source, but what would you do"
" with it?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "separation funnel"
msgid_plural "separation funnels"
msgstr[0] "ampoule à décanter"
msgstr[1] "ampoules à décanter"
msgstr[2] "ampoules à décanter"

#. ~ Description of "separation funnel"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This thing doesn't look much like a funnel.  It's a teardrop shaped piece of"
" glass with a stopper at the wide end and a valve at the other.  It can be "
"used to wash one liquid with another, like water and an oil, and then draw "
"off whichever of the two liquids contains a higher amount of whatever "
"compound you're trying to isolate.  With a high level of skill it can also "
"be used to make juvenile farting noises."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "burette"
msgid_plural "burettes"
msgstr[0] "burette"
msgstr[1] "burettes"
msgstr[2] "burettes"

#. ~ Description of "burette"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A tall glass column with a stopcock at the end.  If you're serious about "
"chemistry, you probably have a tattoo of one of these somewhere."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "rotary evaporator"
msgid_plural "rotary evaporators"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "rotary evaporator"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Just looking at this thing makes you feel like a proper mad scientist.  It's"
" a series of glass tubes and round flasks, connected to a central motor and "
"a heating element.  The heating element warms one flask, kept rotating by "
"the motor, evaporating the contents.  The vapour is then condensed in the "
"tubes and collected in another flask, in case you wanted to save it for "
"later."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "fractional distillation apparatus"
msgid_plural "fractional distillation apparati"
msgstr[0] "appareillage de distillation fractionnée"
msgstr[1] "appareillages de distillation fractionnée"
msgstr[2] "appareillages de distillation fractionnée"

#. ~ Description of "fractional distillation apparatus"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"One of the classic pieces of mad science glassware, this is basically a "
"small volume still that passes the vapour through a fractional distillation "
"column and then condenses the distillate in a cooled collection column.  A "
"grad student or a robot (is there really any difference?) collects the "
"distillate in fractions so that specific contents can be analyzed.  Going a "
"few milliliters at a time, it would not be very effective to try to distill "
"whiskey in this thing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "electrophoresis tray"
msgid_plural "electrophoresis trays"
msgstr[0] "plateau d'électrophorèse"
msgstr[1] "plateaux d'électrophorèse"
msgstr[2] "plateaux d'électrophorèse"

#. ~ Description of "electrophoresis tray"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a set of plastic trays, electrodes, and a power supply designed to "
"create an electric voltage gradient through a liquid solution containing a "
"solid gel.  Stuff like proteins and DNA would then get separated on the gel "
"according to electrical charge and size.  Pretty useless now, for anything "
"but salvage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "microcentrifuge"
msgid_plural "microcentrifuges"
msgstr[0] "microcentrifuge"
msgstr[1] "microcentrifuges"
msgstr[2] "microcentrifuges"

#. ~ Description of "microcentrifuge"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a smaller, benchtop version of the larger furniture-sized "
"centrifuge.  Don't be fooled by its portable scale; it's still a very "
"powerful piece of equipment that can spin stuff really quickly.  It's not a "
"toy!"
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une version de poche, plus petite, de la centrifugeuse de la "
"taille d'un meuble. Ne vous laissez pas tromper par sa taille portable ; "
"c'est tout de même un appareil très puissant qui peut faire tourner des "
"choses très rapidement. Ce n'est pas un jouet !"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "plastic stopcock"
msgid_plural "plastic stopcocks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "plastic stopcock"
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Stop giggling.  This is a tiny plastic valve, get your mind out of the "
"gutter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "test tube rack"
msgid_plural "test tube racks"
